# Cloudflare Pages headers.
#
# Two cache regimes:
#
#   /assets/*        content-hashed names minted by build.sh (nav.a1b2c3d4.js).
#                    The name changes when the content does, so these can be
#                    immutable for a year -- a deploy is still instantly
#                    visible because the pages reference the new names.
#
#   pages + the few  max-age=0 with must-revalidate. That does not mean
#   unversioned      "download every time": the browser sends a conditional
#   scripts          request and gets a 304 when nothing changed, so the cost
#                    is one round trip, and a deploy is visible immediately.
#                    config.js stays here because build.sh injects env values
#                    into it; clarity-init.js because it imports ./vendor by
#                    relative path and so keeps its name.
#
# Images, PDFs and the report covers are deliberately not listed. Those are
# large, they change rarely, and a stale cover is not a broken page.

/assets/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable

/
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=0, must-revalidate

/*.html
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=0, must-revalidate

/config.js
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=0, must-revalidate

/clarity-init.js
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=0, must-revalidate
